export const meta = {
  name: 'swift-harvest',
  description: 'Swift research program phase 6 after a dive wave: one opus agent harvests the new consolidations, appends the landing report to the topic map, applies the stop condition, and commissions the next wave (revised staged briefs plus follow-ups) or declares ready-to-draft with binding authoring notes',
  phases: [{ title: 'Harvest', detail: 'harvest the wave, apply the stop condition, commission the next wave or write the authoring notes', model: 'opus' }],
}

// Generated by mkharvest.py; receipts are baked in because args has a size cap.
const WAVE = __WAVE__
const DATE = '__DATE__'
const RECEIPT = __RECEIPT__
const STAGED = __STAGED__
const ON_DISK = __ON_DISK__

const ROOT = '/home/mherwig/dev/grimoire-lore/.agents/worktrees/swift'
const RESEARCH = ROOT + '/.agents/research'

const SELECTION_ITEM = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    group: { type: 'string', description: 'group slug without the swift- prefix; reuse an existing group slug to make its consolidation a REVISION' },
    group_label: { type: 'string' }, id_family: { type: 'string' },
    slug: { type: 'string' }, label: { type: 'string' },
    brief: { type: 'string', description: '10-25 lines, a professional commission: what to investigate, sources, APIs/compiler flags/lints/versions, exemplar evidence, fixtures to RUN, and what to DECIDE' },
  },
  required: ['group', 'group_label', 'id_family', 'slug', 'label', 'brief'],
}

const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    path: { type: 'string' },
    verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['ready-to-draft', 'needs-another-round'] },
    verdict_reason: { type: 'string' },
    next_wave: { type: 'array', items: SELECTION_ITEM, description: 'empty when ready-to-draft; otherwise at most 14 dives: the staged briefs (revised where wave results changed them) plus follow-ups, each justified by a load-bearing question' },
    frame_corrections: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    rule_totals: { type: 'object', properties: { ids: { type: 'number' }, must: { type: 'number' }, families: { type: 'number' } }, required: ['ids', 'must', 'families'] },
    contradictions_across_consolidations: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
    authoring_notes: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'binding instructions for the phase-7 drafters; may be empty when not ready-to-draft' },
  },
  required: ['path', 'verdict', 'verdict_reason', 'next_wave', 'frame_corrections', 'rule_totals', 'contradictions_across_consolidations', 'authoring_notes'],
}

phase('Harvest')
const r = await agent(`Model rationale: opus — harvesting a wave, the convergence verdict, revising the next wave's commissions and the cross-consolidation contradiction sweep are decisions with a blast radius over every artifact the program ships.

PROJECT CONTEXT (context for you, not content to reproduce):
- You are phase 6 (Iterate) of the research-lang program for Swift and its ecosystem, after dive wave ${WAVE}, run from ${ROOT} (a git worktree; never cd to /home/mherwig/dev/grimoire-lore). The owner set the goal as a fully autonomous run to expertise; the map's owner-question defaults are applied (see the frame's Corrections section: the map's Q1-Q8 defaults).
- Read, in this order and in full: ${ROOT}/.claude/skills/research-lang/SKILL.md (Self-Direction, Phase 6), ${ROOT}/.claude/skills/research-lang/references/wave-plan.md (Convergence), ${ROOT}/.claude/skills/research-lang/references/rule-distillation.md; ${RESEARCH}/swift-frame.md (Corrections and decisions last); ${RESEARCH}/swift-topic-map.md (all of it — the map, Conflicts resolved, Artifact set decision, Staged for wave 3, Deferred, and any earlier "Wave N landed" section); then EVERY consolidation on disk: ${ON_DISK.map(g => RESEARCH + '/swift-' + g + '.md').join(', ')}. Read each in full; the Verdict, ruleset, failure modes and Open questions sections are the material. Open dive files only where a consolidation cites a surprise you must judge.
- Self-direction is the job: every "needs another round" item and every surprise below is a candidate commission. Chase the surprises that are load-bearing. Topics the map never named but the wave surfaced are exactly what the program exists to find.

ORCHESTRATOR FINDINGS SINCE THE WAVE (binding facts; fold them in):
- SwiftLint custom_rules DO work on Linux with a SourceKit-enabled build: the official image ghcr.io/realm/swiftlint:0.65.1 (wrapper /home/mherwig/.cache/research-lang/swift-tools/swiftlint-sk.sh lint --no-cache ...) reported a planted DispatchSemaphore( custom rule as an error (exit 2) and its twin clean (exit 0). The static Linux release binary (on run.sh's PATH as swiftlint) skips custom_rules and every SourceKit rule with only a warning — a silent-green trap that is itself a rule candidate. Fixture: /home/mherwig/.cache/research-lang/swift-tools/fixtures/orch-swiftlint/. This resolves the cli/io/errors follow-ups asking whether custom_rules can carry the grep sets; decide whether gates offers it (advisory vs gate), not whether it works.
- run.sh now passes --security-opt seccomp=unconfined, so swift test --sanitize=thread works in the research toolchain; the Mutex TSan false-positive question is answerable now.
- No macOS, no Windows Swift, no Swift 6.2 image: classify such questions as measurement the corpus cannot supply (owner Q7 default: unverified, read-only).

WAVE ${WAVE} RECEIPT (structured; the files are authoritative where they differ):
${JSON.stringify(RECEIPT, null, 1)}

STAGED NEXT-WAVE BRIEFS FROM THE MAP (revise the ones marked REVISE in light of the wave; keep the rest verbatim unless the wave made them wrong):
${JSON.stringify(STAGED, null, 1)}

DO THREE THINGS.

1. APPEND to ${RESEARCH}/swift-topic-map.md (never rewrite earlier sections) a section "## Wave ${WAVE} landed (${DATE})" with: (a) per group: consolidation path, ID count, MUST count, conflicts resolved, follow-ups named; (b) "Surprises" with a verdict each (promote to next wave / fold into an existing group's revision / defer with M-ID / reject, with the reason); (c) "Map rows affected"; (d) "Frame corrections"; (e) "Cross-consolidation contradictions" — read every ruleset on disk against every other and list each pair that conflicts or overlaps, with the resolution and which ID keeps the text; (f) "Convergence" — apply the wave-plan's stop condition honestly: a wave that still adds MUST rules or new failure modes in freshly opened families has not converged; the clause that decides for the tail is whether any remaining open question is load-bearing AND answerable by a source read or a fixture run. Classify every open question as dated re-check / measurement the corpus cannot supply / owner decision (default applied) / answerable-now. (g) "Next wave" — the full list you return in next_wave, one line each with why; or, if ready-to-draft, "Residue" — what the program deliberately leaves open.

2. If and only if the verdict is ready-to-draft, also append "## Authoring notes (binding on the drafters)": the rules and exact glob lists, the depth files with the ID family each owns and the consolidation sections each draws from, index-owned SW-CORE rules versus depth-owned rules, bounded duplication, the pinned decisions and defaults, the rules to DROP at authoring time with reasons (name IDs), the version-dating convention, the verification-command shape rules (explicit directory operand, one -e per alternative, quoted --include globs, no unquoted **, no $(...), no angle-bracket placeholders inside patterns, xargs -r, no unescaped pipe inside a markdown table cell, what empty output means), the skills' scope (swift-upgrade, swift-diagnose, swift-release: procedures only; any duplicated MUST row appears in a | # | Finding | Rule | table, never as a rule-ID-first row), and the bazel-quality swift.md handoff shape.

3. RETURN the structured receipt. next_wave: when needs-another-round, at most 14 dives total — the staged briefs (revised) plus the follow-ups you promote; a follow-up aimed at a group whose consolidation already exists MUST reuse that group's slug (its consolidation becomes a revision that holds IDs stable); a new group gets a new slug and family. Order it so cross-cutting and revision work comes first. rule_totals counts across every consolidation on disk.

Rules: no claim without a source key, a path, or a rule ID; use read-only tools except for the one append to swift-topic-map.md; do not launch anything; do not edit any consolidation — where two conflict, record the resolution in the append and name which ID's text the drafters keep.`,
  { label: 'harvest:wave' + WAVE, phase: 'Harvest', model: 'opus', effort: 'high', schema: SCHEMA })

if (!r) { log('HARVEST RETURNED NULL — read journal.jsonl'); return { harvest: null } }
log('Verdict: ' + r.verdict + ' · next wave ' + r.next_wave.length + ' · IDs ' + r.rule_totals.ids + ' · MUST ' + r.rule_totals.must + ' · families ' + r.rule_totals.families + ' · contradictions ' + r.contradictions_across_consolidations.length)
return { harvest: r }
